WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:01.700
 Brian.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.102
David.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.437
Congratulations, you've
made it to the final round

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.438
of this competition.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.240
Now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.343
forges where you will recreate
an iconic weapon from history.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:18.584
That weapon is-- a Knights
Templar Crusader Sword.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.687
Good luck Bladesmiths,
we'll see you in five days.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:22.522
 Good luck, man.

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:23.690 line:14%
 Good luck, Brian.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:29.896
 What I am really stoked about
in building the Knights Templar

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.565
Crusader Sword, is the
fact that it's a Knights

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.234
Templar Crusader Sword.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.837
It connects with Christianity
and the religious upbringing

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.339
that I had, it's
really going to be

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.073
rewarding on a lot of levels.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.243
This is the steel I'm going
to use to make my sword.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:47.480
The dimensions that I'm shooting
for are 36 inches in length

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.715
and are under 3 pounds.

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:51.818
I could cut it and forge-weld
it, I could split it,

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:59.024
I could draw it all out, but the
plan is to pull the sword out--

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:00.426
sort of like that.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.995
I have never unfolded
metal this way before

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:06.065
and this is a big
piece of steel.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:07.600
I think I can work with that.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.972
DAVID: The main thing with
the sword is to remove weight.

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:14.941
So we're going to work
on weight reduction

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.610
and get the fuller in there.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:21.147
Just a quick dirty full
of ground in there, man.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.283
I have to start thinking
about my heatery too.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.251
I'm going to have to hook
a burner up to this forge.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.587
People up in Alaska,
more so than many,

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:29.955
we make a lot of our
own tools and equipment.

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:32.725
But really don't
do this at home.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:33.993
It's good to take your time.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.595
Make sure that you
have all the clearance

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:37.830
that you need and then you can
get the piece into the tank.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.098
I don't want to rush anything.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.299
Main thing it's got
to get a good heat

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.867
treatment, the
abuse that they're

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.202
going to put this through.

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:45.905
You can have a disaster
going into the clutch,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.874
I mean, it could
come out all twisted.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.509
We'll just hope that
that doesn't happen.

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.917
So far it looks good.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.787
And it's hard.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.556
So we got a
successful heat-treat.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.824
I'm happy.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.727
It's not a live blade, it
just has to be finished up.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:11.297 line:8%
Can almost see the light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.432 line:8%
BRIAN: I got some
straightening to do.

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:14.934
It's the beginning of day three.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.103
I've got the
profile established.

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:18.938
There's a little bit
of beef here and there

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.174
that needs to come off.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.641
Looking good.

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:24.577
I'm feeling really good
about my blade at this point.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.913
It's to contour,
the follers are cut.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.749
There's only one thing that
I haven't done with my sword

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.317
and that's weigh it.

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:36.289
Oh, we are over 3-pounds,
just with the blade.

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.824
Anything more than
3-pounds places me

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.359
at risk for elimination.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.228
By the time I add a pommal--

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.999
5.5.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.669 line:14%
[beep]

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:51.837
DAVID: This wood that
I'm using right here

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:53.305
is Alaskan Yellow Cedar.

00:02:53.405 --> 00:02:55.040
Really nice wood for handles.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.442
I like it, it's really light.

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.311
Now I've got to make the pommel.

00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:00.145
I've got a long blade out
there, you need something

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:02.148
to counterbalance that.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:03.516
That's what I was looking for--

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.986
a nice piece of wrought
iron, over 100 years old.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.088
Just the right diameter
for the pommel.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.756
That's going to add
weight to the back

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:14.027
and give it some balance.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:17.897
I can't wait to see how
it feels, right now.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.198
Oh, yeah.

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:20.799
It went very well.

00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:23.102
Look at the smile.

00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:25.671
Having my celebratory ice cream.

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.740
My ice cream cosy.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.643
Tomorrow I just expect to put
the final grind on the blade

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.612
and we will be ready
to do some testing.

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.216 line:14%
BRIAN: My blade is almost done.

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:38.517
I drilled my pommel.

00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:40.987
I drilled around the
edge of the pommel.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.189
Ground a little bit
on my cross-guard.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:46.392
I've got my mass down
to around 3-pounds,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.795
but I don't have a
quench on my blade

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.830
yet, that has to happen today.

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:55.268
This is holy water from Chalice
Well in Glastonbury, UK.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.136
This is where
Joseph of Arimathea

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:01.206
allegedly hid the Holy Grail.

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:03.309
Not much, enough to--

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:06.445
enough to bless
the piece though.

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:08.714
I'm ready to go and I'm
scared out of my mind, man.

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:12.018
This is a long blade and
if it goes down the toilet,

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:12.919
I will be gutted.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:23.429
I think we have
a blade, Hoo-yah.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:25.531
The blade is essentially
done at this point.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.634
So it's time to move on to
the pretty parts, the geegaws,

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:29.835
as I call them.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:33.439
Inlays from holy trees, to
the handle, red garnet's

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.307
into the face of
the pommel, this

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:37.443
will symbolize Christ's blood.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.512
There are four real
religious artifacts

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:43.482
included with this piece, not
to mention my own love for it.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:46.385
I feel like I want to
slash at something.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.253
 This is a kill test.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:49.855
A Knights Templar sword.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.958
An iconic weapon battle-tested
throughout history.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:55.761
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:57.429
we'll take your sword
and deliver killing

00:04:57.529 --> 00:04:59.998
blows on this ballistics dummy.

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:01.501
Brian, you're up first.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.502
I would love to test your
blade, but as you can see,

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.038
I'm still recovering
from an injury.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.839
So to be my arm
today, please welcome

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.574
RJ Marcaida, my brother.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.843
He will have the pleasure
of wielding your weapons.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.847
[music playing]

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:33.432
 Your sword is a little
bit on the heavier side,

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:36.101
but because of the pommel
you have over here,

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:38.304
it actually balances it out.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.539
There are areas that
are sharp and there are

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.708
areas that are not as sharp.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:46.312
On the final blow, that edge
have proven to be very sharp

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:49.515
and actually would disembowel
this ballistics dummy.

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:53.285
Your sword sir, will kill.

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.486
All right, David,
it's your turn.

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:55.287
You ready?
- Let's do it

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:58.624
[music playing]

00:06:16.308 --> 00:06:19.245
 That is one of the sharpest
swords I've ever come across.

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:20.813
It's wicked scary.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.549
The cuts lacerated
it almost in half.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:26.285
Without a doubt, your
weapon will kill.

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:27.186
 Awesome.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.988
WILL: Ben.

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:31.691
 Gentlemen to test the strength
and durability of your edges,

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.726
I'm going to attack these
fully armored knights.

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.294
What this test is
all about, what

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.096
the armor does to
your sword, not what

00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:38.331
your sword does to the armor.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:39.431
Brian, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:40.199
 Absolutely.

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:42.935
[music playing]

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.849
 Looks good.

00:06:56.915 --> 00:06:59.752
 Well, Brian, your edge
held up really well.

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:02.621
It's a very obtuse
grind that lends

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:04.056
itself to this kind of test.

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:05.290
The handle was comfortable.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.325
It's a nice shape.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:07.927
I was able to index very well.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:12.098
It stayed straight in the test
and didn't pick up any damage.

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:12.964
Well done.

00:07:13.031 --> 00:07:13.866
 Thank you.

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:14.934
 David, you're up next.

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:17.970
[music playing]

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:33.886
 Well, Dave, you have a
much finer edge on this sword

00:07:33.952 --> 00:07:36.522
and it's picked up a
little bit of rolling.

00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:39.725
There's some edge deflection
right here, you can hear it.

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.494
But all in all, a
very good sword.

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:42.561
 Thank you, sir.

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:43.796
 All right, gentlemen.

00:07:43.862 --> 00:07:45.798
Next up, the swinging
sandbag slice.

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:48.567
I will cut this rope with
one edge of your blade,

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:50.903
releasing that sandbag
and then cutting that

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.638
with the other
edge of your blade.

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.306
Let's see if they
still have an edge.

00:07:54.406 --> 00:07:55.006
Brian, you're up.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:55.741
Are you ready?

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:58.678
[music playing]

00:08:15.827 --> 00:08:20.366
 First off, there are sections
of this blade that just

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:22.268
don't have much of an edge.

00:08:22.368 --> 00:08:24.670
That first cut just
skated up the rope.

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:27.006
A second cut bit in,
went right through.

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:31.543
You can see how there's a lot of
tearing at the edge of that bag

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.547
as opposed to a clean
slice through it.

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:37.349
I would have loved to have
seen a little bit more edge,

00:08:37.415 --> 00:08:40.253
especially on that front half.

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:41.186
David, you ready?

00:08:41.253 --> 00:08:41.887
 Absolutely.

00:08:41.987 --> 00:08:42.454
 OK.

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:45.525
[music playing]

00:08:51.296 --> 00:08:52.297
 Your sword is sharp.

00:08:52.364 --> 00:08:53.465
Very sharp.

00:08:53.565 --> 00:08:55.334
Passed through the
rope, no problem.

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:56.702
Passed through the
bag, no problem.

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:58.604
As far as the design
of your sword,

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:02.141
I would have loved to have
seen a counterbalance on this.

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:05.645
This would be nice on a dagger,
it's very small for this sword.

00:09:05.745 --> 00:09:10.283
Without that counterbalance all
that weight is so far forward,

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:11.249
but it's a cutter.

00:09:11.316 --> 00:09:12.317
It's definitely sharp.

00:09:12.384 --> 00:09:13.084
Nicely done.

00:09:13.151 --> 00:09:14.654
 Thank you.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.289
 Bladesmiths, the judges have
completed their deliberation

00:09:17.356 --> 00:09:18.991
and they've made
a final decision.

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:21.760
You've both put in
a lot of work here.

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:24.363
But there can only be one
Forged in Fire Champion.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:25.831
And that champion is--

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:29.635
Dave.

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:32.605
Congratulations, you are
the Forged in Fire Champion.

00:09:32.671 --> 00:09:35.774
Brian, unfortunately,
your Crusader Sword

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:37.843
did not make the cut.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.345
 Brian, I really applaud the
fact that you brought a lot

00:09:40.412 --> 00:09:41.780
of yourself to that sword.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:44.416
In the end it came down
to your sword just wasn't

00:09:44.482 --> 00:09:46.485
as sharp as your competitors.

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:48.020
And that's why we've
got to let you go.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.354
 Understood.

00:09:49.454 --> 00:09:52.858
 Brian, please
surrender your sword.

00:09:52.924 --> 00:09:55.094
 David's sword cut
better than mine.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.328
He out-smithed me.

00:09:56.428 --> 00:09:57.563
That's the way it goes, man.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.298
In the end there
can be only one.

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:02.668
I may make another Knights
Templar Crusader Sword.

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:06.172
I've still got 2,000-year-old
Oak that's at home.

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:08.674
I still have holy water at home.

00:10:08.741 --> 00:10:11.443
Anything can happen.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.678
 David, congratulations.

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.246
You are the Forged
in Fire Champion.

00:10:14.346 --> 00:10:17.182
And that's a title that comes
with a check for how much?

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:18.050
 10 grand.

00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:19.151
 That's right. $10,000.

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:21.286
Good job.

00:10:21.353 --> 00:10:22.654
 Victory feels good.

00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:24.256
In this competition,
it showed me

00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:28.027
that I can push myself a little
harder and maybe get more done.

00:10:28.093 --> 00:10:29.862
Looking forward to
getting back home.

00:10:29.929 --> 00:10:33.031
First thing I'm going to do is
fix my bike and go for a ride.

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:36.168
[music playing]

